flowchart TB

CHOICE["`MONOLITH OR MICROSERVICES?
microservices sell scale and independent
deploys, but charge for it with distribution,
complexity and operational load —
heavy for a small team and a product
still being validated`"]

MONO["`MODULAR MONOLITH — the middle ground
one repository · one deploy
code fully split into modules
boundaries held by the CODE, not the network
15,160 lines of Python`"]

CUT["`A DELIBERATE LOOSE END
module boundaries drawn exactly where
a future cut into services would happen —
that option stays open`"]

DDD["`13 MODULES — DDD-inspired
folder structure and layers, yes
Value Objects and ubiquitous language, no —
exactly the concepts that made sense here`"]

P["`presentation/
HTTP and nothing else
routes · request and response shapes`"]

A["`application/
services · use cases
business rules`"]

D["`domain/
pure Python
entities · enums · interfaces · exceptions
no framework, no database —
would survive FastAPI and SQLAlchemy
disappearing from the project`"]

I["`infrastructure/
SQLAlchemy · queries
adapters to the outside world`"]

RULE["`DEPENDENCY RULE — a cascade
only outer layers may know inner ones,
never the reverse: the domain has no idea
what HTTP or a database is`"]

OWN["`OWNERSHIP INVARIANT — strict multitenancy
every domain query is scoped to the
authenticated owner · the user id NEVER
comes from the request body, always from
Bearer Authorization · vector search refuses
to run without a valid scope`"]

CHOICE --> MONO
MONO -.- CUT
MONO --> DDD
DDD --> P
P -->|"may know"| A
A -->|"may know"| D
I -->|"adapts for"| D
P -.- RULE
OWN -.->|"enforced across all 13 modules"| DDD

